The STACKIT landing zone `${platform_identifier}` is ready.

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Organization | `${organization_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${organization_url})) |
%{ if root_folder_name != "" ~}
| Root Folder | `${root_folder_name}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${root_folder_url})) |
%{ endif ~}
| Landing Zone Folder | `${lz_folder_container_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${lz_folder_url})) |
| Foundation Project | `${foundation_project_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${foundation_project_url})) |
| Foundation Project Service Account | `${service_account_email}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${service_account_url})) |
%{ if network_enabled ~}
| Hub Network Area | `${network_area_id}` ([Open in STACKIT Portal](${network_area_url})) |
| Hub Network Area Building Block | @buildingblock[${network_area_hub_uuid}] |
| Spoke Landing Zone | `${spoke_landingzone_name}` |
%{ endif ~}

%{ if network_enabled ~}
Hub&spoke networking is enabled. Application teams can now add *STACKIT Project* from the
marketplace to their tenants. On the `${spoke_landingzone_name}` landing zone it also orders a
spoke *STACKIT Network*, drawn from the hub's address plan.
%{ else ~}
Application teams can now add *STACKIT Project* from the marketplace to their tenants on the
`${platform_identifier}-default` landing zone. Add `hub&spoke` to the topology to also enable
hub&spoke networking.
%{ endif ~}

> [!TIP]
> # Build a Kubernetes platform on top
>
> The [STACKIT Kubernetes Platform](https://hub.meshcloud.io/reference-architectures/stackit-kubernetes)
> reference architecture runs a full SKE developer platform on top of this landing zone. It takes one
> value from this landing zone. Paste this block into its *STACKIT Landing Zone* input:
>
> ```hcl
> {
>   platform_ref = { uuid = "${platform_ref.uuid}" }
>   landingzone_refs = {
%{ for key, ref in landingzone_refs ~}
>     ${key} = { name = "${ref.name}" }
%{ endfor ~}
>   }
>   project_bbd_version_ref                    = { uuid = "${project_bbd_version_uuid}" }
>   service_account_bbd_version_ref            = { uuid = "${service_account_bbd_version_uuid}" }
>   service_account_federation_bbd_version_ref = { uuid = "${service_account_federation_bbd_version_uuid}" }
> }
> ```
%{ if network_enabled ~}
>
> Set its *Landing Zone Variant* to `spoke` to run the cluster inside the hub&spoke network.
> Otherwise keep the default `default`, which puts the cluster in a *STACKIT Sandbox* project with
> STACKIT's default flat networking.
%{ endif ~}
%{ if !composed_definitions_released ~}

> [!NOTE]
> Not all latest versions of the *STACKIT Project*, *STACKIT Service Account* and *STACKIT
> Service Account Federation* definitions are released, so only this workspace can order them. To
> order them from another workspace, deploy this landing zone with `hub.bbd_draft = false` and
> `release_service_account_bbds = true`, publish the three definitions to the marketplace, then run
> this building block again.
%{ endif ~}
%{ if playground_mode ~}

*Playground mode:* the platform identifier carries a random suffix and nothing here is protected
against deletion, so publish this platform or its building block definitions only to test that path.
Redeploy with `playground_mode` set to false for a platform that is actually used.
%{ endif ~}
